cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Entropy Self-Estimation Lab"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end experiment testing whether language models can estimate
  the true entropy of their own sampling distribution beyond what is
  inferable from visible text. Includes absolute and pairwise comparative
  judgment paradigms, local transformers/GGUF engines, a remote
  OpenAI-compatible engine (LM Studio), and a web interface.
authors:
  - family-names: "Entropy Self-Estimation Lab"
    given-names: "Contributors"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/msalsas/entropy-lab"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - introspection
  - sampling entropy
  - verbalized uncertainty
  - metacognition
